  "description": "EZIDOJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C114 H98 Gd4 N6 O24,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.705-3.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.84-113.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C116H106Gd4N6O26.",
